---
/**
 * /help — Help / about page.
 *
 * Restructured in slice 26d: each top-level section (intro, quick links,
 * FAQs, need-more-help) gets its own card so the page is scannable
 * instead of reading as one long prose block. FAQs use native
 * <details>/<summary> for collapsible answers — no JS needed, works
 * without hydration.
 *
 * Slice 7 (release/astro-migration) closed the visible 404 from
 * `MoreSheet.tsx:133` (`closeAndNavigate('/help')`). The mobile More
 * sheet's "Help" item used to dead-end at 404 because no page existed.
 *
 * Auth: the Astro middleware does NOT require auth for /help (it's a
 * "public documentation" page, like /terms and /privacy).
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '../components/ui/card';
---

<Layout title="Help — Castor" description="Help and resources for Castor.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 flex flex-col gap-8">

    <PageHeader
      title="Help"
      back="/"
      subtitle="Documentation and resources for Castor."
    />

    {/* ── Intro card ── */}
    <Card className="w-full">
      <CardContent className="pt-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Castor is self-hostable, so the docs live with the project.
        Below are the quickest ways to get unstuck, plus answers
        to questions that come up often.
      </CardContent>
    </Card>

    {/* ── Quick links ── */}
    <Card className="w-full">
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Quick links</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent className="grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/beaverhabits/castor/wiki"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          class="block rounded-md border border-border px-3 py-2.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent transition-colors"
        >
          <span class="font-semibold block">Wiki</span>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">Usage guides, screenshots, and how-tos.</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/sponsors/beaverhabits"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          class="block rounded-md border border-border px-3 py-2.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent transition-colors"
        >
          <span class="font-semibold block">Support Castor</span>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">The project is self-hosted by the maintainer.</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.youtube.com/@beaverhabits"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          class="block rounded-md border border-border px-3 py-2.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent transition-colors"
        >
          <span class="font-semibold block">YouTube channel</span>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">Short walkthrough videos.</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/beaverhabits/castor/issues"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          class="block rounded-md border border-border px-3 py-2.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent transition-colors"
        >
          <span class="font-semibold block">Issue tracker</span>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">Bug reports and feature requests.</span>
        </a>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>

    {/* ── FAQ (collapsible) ── */}
    <Card className="w-full">
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Frequently asked questions</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent className="divide-y divide-border">
        <details class="group py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 font-medium">
            How is my data stored?
            <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Your habit data lives in a SQLite database on the server that
            runs Castor. Each user's data is isolated by user_id; the
            server never shares it with other users or third parties.
            Backups are the operator's responsibility.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 font-medium">
            Can I export my data?
            <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Yes. Go to <a href="/export" class="underline">Export</a> to
            download a JSON snapshot of all your habits, ticks, and
            notes. The file can be re-imported on another device via
            <a href="/import" class="underline">Import</a>.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 font-medium">
            Can I import from another tool?
            <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            The <a href="/import" class="underline">Import</a> page
            accepts JSON snapshots in the Castor / beaverhabits format.
            CSV import is not currently supported.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 font-medium">
            What if I lose my passkey?
            <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            If you registered a recovery email on the
            <a href="/security" class="underline">Security</a> page, you
            can use the <a href="/forgot-password" class="underline">Forgot password</a>
            flow to receive a 12-digit code and reset your password.
            Without a recovery email (and without a working password),
            the operator must intervene directly on the database —
            there is no self-service bypass by design.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 font-medium">
            Why is the Astro UI slower than the old NiceGUI app?
            <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Each Astro page is server-rendered. The first request
            after a navigation fetches fresh data; subsequent requests
            in the same session are fast. Mobile users on flaky
            networks may notice the extra round-trip compared to the
            old single-page-app model.
          </p>
        </details>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>

    {/* ── Need more help ── */}
    <Card className="w-full">
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>Need more help?</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Open an issue on the
          <a
            href="https://github.com/beaverhabits/castor/issues"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
            class="underline ml-1"
          >issue tracker</a>
          and the maintainer will respond.
        </p>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>

  </main>
</Layout>
